--- Runs a side-effect function on a value, then returns the value unchanged.
---
--- @details
--- `tap` takes `[f, x]`, evaluates `f(x)` for its effect, and yields `x`.
--- It lets you observe or log a value mid-pipeline without altering the
--- data flowing through.
---
--- The result of `f` is discarded; `f` is expected to be effectful.
---
--- @example
--- `[x ~> print(x), 42] >>> comb.tap`
--- -- => 42
---
export tap :: [f, x]~> do {
  f(x)
  x
}
